// Two lesions that merge, seen through footprint labelling (option A of the
// note): the case A gets wrong. The series is frames/merge_<t>.png, drawn in
// frames/draw.py together with the expected result.
//
// merged(l) holds, at frame t, on the component of the lesion at t+1 that
// touches region l at t and also touches a lesion at t outside region l: a
// merge that involves l. The footprint is the lcc of the union of the lesion
// over the whole series, so the two lesions of frame 0, joined at frame 1,
// are one footprint component from the start: region 1 is both of them, no
// lesion lies outside it, and the merge is invisible. Expected: false
// everywhere (frames/merge-footprint.expected.png).
let video = load("merge")
let lesion = gt(intensity(frame(video,n)),127)
let footprint = initially(lcc(until(true,lesion)))
let region(l) = and(eq(footprint,l),lesion)
let merged(l) = and(through(region(l),diamond(lesion)),through(and(lesion,not(region(l))),diamond(lesion)))
save "merge-footprint" exists(l,footprint,merged(l))
